      "notes": "All claims are well-anchored to their cited evidence and tiers are correctly assigned. The E23 claim is labelled measurable (House of Lords committee concern), which is appropriate as a documented parliamentary position rather than a projection. The E16 claim (Farage/sovereignty) is correctly labelled projected and scoped to 'earlier versions', matching the quote. The Bank of England privacy assurance (E27) is correctly labelled projected. The direction 'improves/minor' is justified primarily by the CBDC/cashless planks; the WHO/WEF elements are correctly assessed as negligible for O10 with no unsupported liberty mechanism claimed. No party-blind issues: the rationale judges effect, not motive. No false balance: the verdict reaches 'improves' with genuine evidence on both sides (surveillance risk vs. Bank of England privacy assurances) and correctly characterises the gain as minor. Magnitude and time_horizon are proportionate given the CBDC is not yet approved. No lever leakage detected \u2014 sovereignty is treated as context, not scored for its own sake."
